+## P14 — qualification in progress, 6 November 2026
+
+Working version remains **1.8.8**. Current native source is
+`d4e48a534881ea910bcbadd182e8fb4f6a970c844df6ab1951d7b566cbcb2eeb`
+(**960** declared inputs). This is a new production source: Kernel's semantic-ready
+DestinationBuild path now uses the canonical bundled-model selection/provisioning
+owner before Current initialization and indexing. P12's accepted `4121692a…` pair
+is historical evidence and cannot qualify this production correction.
+
+The actual cold-default failure reached a native split child that could not prove
+semantic readiness. Source-only indexing had no installed default reference and
+correctly did not provision one implicitly. The correction selects the paired
+default through the existing claimed owner. It does not increase the 32-turn
+semantic bound or weaken ready/publication checks. The new fixture first proves
+that no default reference is installed. Earlier R1–R4 diagnostic attempts and their
+failed receipts retain their original outcomes; no later pass relabels them.
+
+Observed current-source evidence:
+
+- Full Windows Nextest: **2,624 passed**, **50 selection exclusions**; all four
+  previously excluded long workload cases were restored and passed.
+- Strict workspace all-target/all-feature Clippy passed. The final Windows
+  release qualification passed **15/15** stages, including actual semantic-ready
+  split, existing provider split, reference refresh and retention transport cases.
+- Full extension suite: **776 passed, 19 skipped** out of **795** tests.
+- Scoped Neo source batch: formatting plus **two actual integration cases** passed.
+  The semantic-ready destination used the bundled ARM default; the lexical case
+  retained its existing behavior. `cargo clean` exited **0**, timing reports were
+  retained and the target was absent afterward. This is not a full Mac workspace
+  or installed-editor/signing result.
+
+**Pending broader outcomes — replace only from collected actual receipts:**
+scale/resource, service/load, installed-native, upgrade, transformer/code/retrieval,
+storage/usage and ignored vector-performance campaigns remain under collection.
+The 10,000-file scale driver encountered supported `selection_busy` while polling;
+its read-retry harness correction is under review. This is not evidence of an
+index-capacity or production service defect, and no successful 10k outcome is claimed.
+Remaining campaigns may finish independently; collect their complete results before
+applying a correction or repeating a failed campaign.
+
+**Pending external/installed outcomes:** real-corpus comparisons, current VSIX and
+legacy/editor flows, Linux/container, additional installed platforms and signing
+remain unqualified. Docker's Linux amd64 engine is reachable but has no cached
+images; no Linux build/container pass is inferred. No publication or ordinary
+user installation is authorized by these local results.
+
+**Acceptance placeholder:** P14 is **in progress, not accepted**. Record final
+resource/platform outcomes and primary review here before changing that state.
+After P14, the separately reviewed deleted-source recovery proposal still needs
+application and actual Windows/Neo isolation, lease and retirement qualification.
+It is not included in this source and must precede the final local test installer.
